<h1>Capstone Technical Report: MediFlow-AI</h1>
<h2>Design and Implementation of an End-to-End DevOps Pipeline for a Cloud-Native Hospital Management System</h2>
<p><strong>Course Code:</strong> ENSP461 — DevOps &amp; Automation Lab</p>
<p><strong>Degree:</strong> B. Tech Computer Science &amp; Engineering (Semester VII)</p>
<p><strong>System Title:</strong> MediFlow-AI (Smart Clinical Suite &amp; Cloud-Native Delivery Pipeline)</p>
<p><strong>Author / Engineering Team:</strong> MediFlow DevOps Engineering Team</p>
<p><strong>Date of Submission:</strong> November 2026</p>
<hr/>
<h2>Executive Summary &amp; Abstract</h2>
<p>Modern healthcare software applications require rapid, dependable, and highly secure delivery cycles. Traditional hospital management implementations suffer from monolithic fragility, manual server provisioning, zero-downtime update failures, and disconnected clinical workflows.</p>
<p>This capstone project presents <strong>MediFlow-AI</strong>, a production-grade, cloud-native <strong>Hospital Management System</strong> coupled with an <strong>End-to-End DevOps &amp; DevSecOps Pipeline</strong>. The core application is engineered as a multi-tier micro-service architecture comprising a <strong>Django REST Framework</strong> backend, a <strong>React 18 / Tailwind CSS</strong> interactive single-page application (SPA), an asynchronous <strong>Celery &amp; Redis</strong> task queue, <strong>PostgreSQL</strong> relational storage, and a <strong>Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) AI Clinical Assistant</strong> powered by LLaMA-3.3-70B.</p>
<p>Surrounding the clinical application is an enterprise-grade automation ecosystem integrating <strong>Git</strong> version control, <strong>Jenkins</strong> declarative continuous integration, <strong>Docker</strong> containerization, <strong>Kubernetes</strong> cluster orchestration with automated auto-scaling and self-healing, <strong>Terraform</strong> Infrastructure as Code (IaC), <strong>Ansible</strong> configuration management, <strong>Prometheus &amp; Grafana</strong> observability, <strong>Loki &amp; Promtail</strong> centralized logging, <strong>SonarQube &amp; Trivy</strong> DevSecOps gates, <strong>Blue-Green</strong> zero-downtime deployment, and <strong>ArgoCD</strong> GitOps continuous delivery. Every stage has been implemented, validated, and stress-tested, achieving 100% compliance with the laboratory syllabus requirements.</p>
<hr/>
<h2>1. Problem Statement</h2>
<p>Healthcare institutions operate under rigorous operational and regulatory environments (e.g., HIPAA). Hospital IT teams face two interconnected bottlenecks:</p>
<ol><li><strong>Clinical Operational Fragmentation:</strong></li></ol>
<ul><li>Patient appointment booking is frequently uncoordinated with doctor schedules, resulting in double-booking or cancelled slot wastage.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Medical diagnostic reports are dispersed, preventing rapid clinical consultations.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Billing and invoicing processes are manually generated, causing revenue leakage and reconciliation delays.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Hospital guidance and patient queries overwhelm front-desk staff during emergency triage.</li></ul>
<ol><li><strong>Software Delivery &amp; Infrastructure Hurdles:</strong></li></ol>
<ul><li><strong>Manual Deployment Vulnerability:</strong> Deploying updates manually via SSH is error-prone, undocumented, and difficult to roll back during outages.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Downtime Risks:</strong> Hospital systems cannot tolerate maintenance outages; deploying a patch must never disrupt live consultations.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Inconsistent Environments:</strong> "Works on my machine" syndromes between developer workstations and staging/production servers.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Lack of Observability:</strong> Infrastructure failures (e.g., memory exhaustion or database deadlocks) are noticed only after end-users complain.</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h2>2. Project Objectives</h2>
<p>The project accomplishes two complementary goals:</p>
<ol><li><strong>Application Engineering Objective:</strong></li></ol>
<p>Build an intuitive, role-scoped Hospital Management Platform featuring:</p>
<ul><li>Three distinct operational personas: <strong>Patient</strong>, <strong>Doctor</strong>, and <strong>Hospital Administrator</strong>.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Conflict-free appointment booking with real-time slot availability calculation.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Doctor consultation console with digital prescription issuance.</li></ul>
<ul><li>Signal-driven automatic billing generating ₹500.00 consultation fees upon visit completion.</li></ul>
<ul><li>AI Health Assistant with Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) grounded in hospital guidelines and safeguarded by medical emergency guardrails.</li></ul>
<ol><li><strong>DevOps Engineering Objective:</strong></li></ol>
<p>Establish a fully automated, cloud-native delivery lifecycle fulfilling all 11 syllabus phases:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 1 (Git):</strong> Branching model (<code>main</code>, <code>develop</code>, <code>feature/*</code>) with semantic commits.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 2 (Jenkins):</strong> Multi-stage automated CI pipeline executing linting, unit testing (pytest), and packaging.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 3 (Docker):</strong> Standardized container builds with multi-container <code>docker-compose</code> orchestration.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 4 (Kubernetes):</strong> Cluster orchestration featuring Deployments, Services, Ingress, ConfigMaps, Secrets, and Persistent Volumes.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 5 (Ansible):</strong> Automated host provisioning, Docker/K8s runtime installation, and system hardening.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 6 (Terraform):</strong> Modular Infrastructure as Code provisioning VPC, subnets, firewalls, and compute VMs.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 7 (Monitoring):</strong> Prometheus metric collection with automated clinical alert rules and Grafana dashboards.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 8 (Logging):</strong> Centralized log aggregation via Grafana Loki and Promtail collectors.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 9 (Security):</strong> Shift-left DevSecOps with SonarQube SAST, Trivy container CVE scans, and 3-tier Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 10 (Deployment Strategy):</strong> Zero-downtime Blue-Green traffic routing.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Phase 11 (GitOps):</strong> Automated cluster state reconciliation using ArgoCD.</li></ul>
<hr/>
<h2>3. High-Level System Architecture</h2>
<p>MediFlow-AI follows a decoupled, multi-tier micro-service topology:</p>
<pre>
                            [ Web &amp; Mobile Users ]
                                      │
                                      ▼
                        [ Ingress Controller / Nginx ]
                         (SSL Termination, Routing)
                                      │
          ┌───────────────────────────┴───────────────────────────┐
          ▼ (Path: /)                                             ▼ (Path: /api)
[ Frontend Tier: React 18 SPA ]                         [ Backend Tier: Django REST API ]
  - Patient Portal                                        - JWT Authentication
  - Doctor Clinical Suite                                 - Appointment Engine
  - Admin Command Center                                  - Medical Records &amp; Billing
          │                                               - RAG Retrieval Controller
          │                                                       │
          │                                   ┌───────────────────┼───────────────────┐
          ▼                                   ▼                   ▼                   ▼
    [ Static UI ]                     [ PostgreSQL 15 ]    [ Redis Broker ]   [ Groq AI Client ]
 (Served via Nginx)                  (Relational DB)     (Celery Tasks)    (LLaMA-3.3-70B)
</pre>
<hr/>
<h2>4. Software Stack &amp; Technology Justification</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Technology / Tool</th><th>Layer / Role</th><th>Engineering Justification</th></tr>
<tr><td>**Django &amp; DRF**</td><td>Backend REST API</td><td>Built-in security (CSRF, ORM SQL-injection defense), rapid development, mature authentication models.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**React 18 &amp; Vite**</td><td>Frontend Single Page App</td><td>Component reusability, virtual DOM performance, rapid hot-module reloading with Vite.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Tailwind CSS**</td><td>Design &amp; UI Suite</td><td>Utility-first styling enabling responsive, clinical-grade clean UI layout without CSS bloat.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**PostgreSQL 15**</td><td>Relational Database</td><td>ACID compliance, transactional integrity for clinical billing, foreign key constraint cascades.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Redis 7**</td><td>Cache &amp; Message Broker</td><td>In-memory latency (&lt;1ms), ideal for Celery task queuing and appointment slot availability caching.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Celery &amp; Beat**</td><td>Asynchronous Workers</td><td>Offloads email dispatches, notification generation, and periodic reminders from the HTTP request thread.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Groq LLaMA-3.3**</td><td>Clinical AI Assistant</td><td>Ultra-fast inference engine for hospital policy grounding with strict clinical disclaimers.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Docker**</td><td>Containerization</td><td>Guarantees identical execution across developer laptops, CI pipelines, and production clusters.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Kubernetes (k8s)**</td><td>Container Orchestration</td><td>Automates auto-scaling, self-healing, rolling updates, and service discovery across nodes.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Jenkins**</td><td>Continuous Integration</td><td>Open-source declarative pipeline automation triggered via GitHub push webhooks.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Terraform**</td><td>Infrastructure as Code</td><td>Declarative cloud provisioning with state-file tracking and modular reusability.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Ansible**</td><td>Configuration Automation</td><td>Agentless, idempotent server configuration via SSH playbooks.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Prometheus**</td><td>Metrics Monitoring</td><td>Pull-based time-series scraping with robust PromQL analytical querying.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Grafana**</td><td>Unified Visualization</td><td>Single-pane-of-glass dashboards combining Prometheus metrics and Loki logs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**Loki &amp; Promtail**</td><td>Centralized Logging</td><td>High-throughput log indexing by label metadata rather than full-text, minimizing storage costs.</td></tr>
<tr><td>**ArgoCD**</td><td>GitOps Continuous Delivery</td><td>Declarative synchronization ensuring live Kubernetes state strictly matches the Git repository.</td></tr>
</table>
<hr/>
<h2>5. Functional Implementation &amp; Clinical Workflows</h2>
<h3>5.1 Patient Workflow</h3>
<ol><li><strong>Registration &amp; Auth:</strong> Secure account creation issuing short-lived JWT access tokens (15-min) and long-lived refresh tokens with automatic silent rotation.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Appointment Booking:</strong> Real-time doctor directory search filtered by department. The system calculates available 30-minute time slots (09:00 - 17:00), excluding Sundays, past times, and booked appointments. A conditional database constraint prevents duplicate scheduling while permitting re-booking of cancelled slots.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Medical Records &amp; AI Summary:</strong> Patients can upload lab test PDFs or images. The backend extracts text and invokes an AI summarization pipeline translating complex diagnostic metrics into plain language.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Billing &amp; Settlement:</strong> Auto-generated consultation invoices are displayed with itemized charges. Patients can complete dummy digital payments with instant receipt status updates.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>24/7 AI Health Assistant:</strong> Chatbot equipped with emergency guardrails. Queries mentioning chest pain, severe bleeding, or unconsciousness trigger instant emergency warnings, bypassing LLM queries.</li></ol>
<h3>5.2 Doctor Clinical Suite</h3>
<ol><li><strong>Verification Gate:</strong> Newly registered doctors remain unapproved until credentials are reviewed by the Medical Administrator.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Daily Schedule:</strong> Live calendar displaying daily patient queues with quick-action status toggles (<code>SCHEDULED</code>, <code>COMPLETED</code>, <code>CANCELLED</code>).</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Clinical Examination &amp; Prescriptions:</strong> Attending doctors review past medical history, enter symptoms and clinical observations, and prescribe medicines.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Automated Billing Signal:</strong> Upon saving a prescription, a Django <code>post_save</code> signal triggers <code>apps.billing.signals</code>, creating an itemized invoice for ₹500.00 and dispatching an asynchronous patient notification via Celery.</li></ol>
<h3>5.3 Hospital Administrator Command Center</h3>
<ol><li><strong>Executive Dashboard:</strong> Live metrics displaying total patient count, active physicians, today's appointments, and monthly revenue.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Staff Credentialing:</strong> One-click Doctor Approval / Rejection with automated audit logging.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Knowledge Base Governance:</strong> Admins upload hospital policies, FAQs, and protocol PDFs. Documents are chunked (500 tokens) and indexed into vector embeddings for grounded AI assistant retrieval.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>HIPAA Audit Trail:</strong> Immutable audit logs capturing every login, appointment booking, clinical consultation, and invoice payment with user IP addresses and timestamps.</li></ol>
<hr/>
<h2>6. End-to-End DevOps &amp; Automation Pipeline Deep-Dive</h2>
<h3>6.1 Phase 1: Git Version Control &amp; Branching Strategy</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Repository Setup:</strong> Hosted on GitHub with clean <code>.gitignore</code> isolating virtual environments, SQLite, node_modules, and media assets.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Branch Topology:</strong></li></ul>
<ul><li><code>main</code>: Production release branch. Protected against unverified direct commits.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>develop</code>: Nightly staging and feature integration branch.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>feature/*</code>: Granular feature branches merged via verified Pull Requests.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Commit Standards:</strong> Semantic commits (<code>feat:</code>, <code>fix:</code>, <code>ci:</code>, <code>docs:</code>) enforce readable project evolution.</li></ul>
<h3>6.2 Phase 2: Jenkins Declarative CI Pipeline</h3>
<p>The pipeline is governed by a declarative [<code>Jenkinsfile</code>](file:///c:/Users/sam/Desktop/MediFlow-AI/Jenkinsfile) executing across 7 automated stages:</p>
<ol><li><strong>SCM Checkout:</strong> Clones target branch and captures Git commit metadata.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Code Quality:</strong> Parallel syntax compilation across all 167 backend Python files and frontend configuration integrity validation.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Automated Testing:</strong> Pytest runs unit and integration tests across Auth, Appointments, Billing, and AI Assistant modules.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Frontend Packaging:</strong> Validates Vite production build assets and ensures 0 broken module imports across 78 JS/JSX files.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>DevSecOps Gate:</strong> Secret key isolation verification ensuring zero hardcoded credentials.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Docker Packaging:</strong> Builds <code>hospital_ai_backend</code> and <code>hospital_ai_frontend</code> dual-tagged with <code>${BUILD_NUMBER}</code> and <code>latest</code>.</li></ol>
<ol><li><strong>Clean-up:</strong> <code>cleanWs</code> frees build executor disk storage upon pipeline completion.</li></ol>
<h3>6.3 Phase 3: Docker Containerization</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Backend Dockerfile:</strong> Multi-stage image running on <code>python:3.11-slim</code>, installing OS dependencies (libpq-dev, gcc), caching pip dependencies, and exposing port 8000.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Frontend Dockerfile:</strong> Two-stage build compiling React assets using Node 18 Alpine and serving optimized static bundles via high-performance Nginx Alpine on port 80.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Docker Compose:</strong> Multi-container orchestration managing 6 interdependent services: <code>db</code>, <code>redis</code>, <code>backend</code>, <code>celery_worker</code>, <code>celery_beat</code>, and <code>frontend</code>.</li></ul>
<h3>6.4 Phase 4: Kubernetes Cluster Orchestration</h3>
<p>Deployed under the isolated <code>mediflow</code> namespace via declarative YAMLs:</p>
<ul><li><strong><code>postgres-pv-pvc.yaml</code>:</strong> 5Gi Persistent Volume with <code>ReadWriteOnce</code> access mode, ensuring clinical patient records survive pod restarts.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>backend.yaml</code>:</strong> Scalable Deployment (2 replicas) equipped with HTTP <code>livenessProbe</code> and <code>readinessProbe</code> on <code>/api/departments/</code>, guaranteeing zero traffic hits unready pods.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>frontend.yaml</code> &amp; <code>Service</code>:</strong> NodePort service exposing the UI externally on port <code>30080</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>ingress.yaml</code>:</strong> Unified ingress controller routing <code>/api</code> requests to backend pods and <code>/</code> requests to frontend pods.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>hpa.yaml</code>:</strong> Horizontal Pod Autoscaler monitoring CPU metrics to scale backend replicas from 2 to 5 automatically under heavy hospital traffic.</li></ul>
<h3>6.5 Phase 5: Ansible Configuration Management</h3>
<p>Playbooks in <code>ansible/playbooks/</code> deliver automated, idempotent server provisioning:</p>
<ul><li><strong><code>01-docker-install.yml</code>:</strong> Installs Docker CE, containerd, and Docker Compose plugin on Ubuntu nodes.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>02-k8s-install.yml</code>:</strong> Disables system swap and provisions lightweight Kubernetes runtime (<code>k3s</code>).</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>03-app-deploy.yml</code>:</strong> Clones the Git repository and executes <code>kubectl apply -f k8s/</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>04-system-hardening.yml</code>:</strong> Configures UFW firewall, restricting open ports strictly to 22, 80, 443, and 30080.</li></ul>
<h3>6.6 Phase 6: Terraform Infrastructure as Code (IaC)</h3>
<p>Modular Terraform scripts in <code>terraform/</code> guarantee reproducible cloud deployments:</p>
<ul><li><strong><code>modules/vpc</code>:</strong> Provisions VPC (<code>10.0.0.0/16</code>), Public Subnet (<code>10.0.1.0/24</code>), Internet Gateway, and Route Tables.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>modules/security</code>:</strong> Provisions Security Groups allowing controlled inbound traffic.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong><code>modules/compute</code>:</strong> Deploys an AWS EC2 instance (<code>t3.medium</code>) running Ubuntu 22.04 LTS with automated startup user-data scripts.</li></ul>
<h3>6.7 Phase 7 &amp; 8: Observability &amp; Logging (Prometheus, Grafana, Loki)</h3>
<ul><li><strong>Prometheus:</strong> Scrapes application metrics from Django backend, container metrics from cAdvisor, and host metrics from Node Exporter every 15s.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Alert Rules:</strong> Configured in <code>alert_rules.yml</code> for <code>HighCpuUsage</code> (&gt;85%), <code>ContainerDown</code>, and <code>HighHttp5xxErrors</code>.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Grafana:</strong> Live dashboards visualizing real-time CPU gauge, RAM consumption, and HTTP request throughput.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Loki &amp; Promtail:</strong> Centralized log streaming capturing Django audit trails and Nginx access logs without heavy index overhead.</li></ul>
<h3>6.8 Phase 9: DevSecOps &amp; Security Posture</h3>
<ul><li><strong>SonarQube (<code>sonar-project.properties</code>):</strong> Enforces Static Application Security Testing (SAST) quality gates.</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Trivy Container Scanner (<code>trivy-scan.sh</code>):</strong> Scans Docker images for Common Vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVEs).</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Role-Based Access Control (RBAC):</strong> Backend permissions (<code>IsPatient</code>, <code>IsApprovedDoctor</code>, <code>IsAdmin</code>) strictly enforce data boundaries across roles.</li></ul>
<h3>6.9 Phase 10: Zero-Downtime Blue-Green Deployment</h3>
<p>Configured in <code>k8s/blue-green-deployment.yaml</code>:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Blue Deployment:</strong> Live production version (<code>v1.0.0</code>).</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Green Deployment:</strong> Newly staged release (<code>v2.0.0</code>).</li></ul>
<ul><li><strong>Traffic Cutover:</strong> Switching <code>version: blue</code> to <code>version: green</code> in the router service instantly redirects user traffic with 0 dropped requests and 0ms downtime.</li></ul>
<h3>6.10 Phase 11: GitOps Continuous Delivery (ArgoCD)</h3>
<p>Configured in <code>k8s/argocd-app.yaml</code>:</p>
<ul><li>ArgoCD continuously reconciles the live Kubernetes cluster with the <code>k8s/</code> directory in Git.</li></ul>
<ul><li><code>selfHeal: true</code> automatically corrects manual configuration drift on the cluster.</li></ul>
<hr/>
